[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2970124315","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107481#issuecomment-2970124315","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107481","id":2970124315,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xCIAb","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-13T11:38:05Z","updated_at":"2025-06-13T11:38:05Z","body":"> Instead of relying on the ability of linked list to remove an element fast, we use `remove_at_unordered` to remove elements in O(1). With linear lists, and keeping an ID of which child we are in the parent list, we have to rejig the child that is moved during `remove_at_unordered()`, and reassign its child ID. That should be the only thing required to keep the IDs in sync.\r\n\r\nI might be missing something here, but isn't this a pretty serious change? Moving nodes around changes their processing order, and in the case of 2D their drawing order.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2970124315/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2970127753","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107481#issuecomment-2970127753","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107481","id":2970127753,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xCI2J","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-13T11:39:44Z","updated_at":"2025-06-13T13:43:17Z","body":"> I might be missing something here, but isn't this a pretty serious change? Moving nodes around changes their processing order, and in the case of 2D their drawing order.\r\n\r\nYou are missing something. Draw / processing order is determined by `Node` children, not `CanvasItem` children.\r\n\r\nIt's a peculiar arrangement. The `Spatial` children and `CanvasItem` children are a subset of the actual `Node` children, and they are unordered. They are used for propagating transforms and a few other flags.\r\n\r\nThere's only about 5 or so uses of the `Spatial` and `CanvasItem` children, and they aren't exposed - they are purely a \"difficult to notice\" internal optimization that was introduced when Godot went open source. I may be able to use them for `SceneTreeFTI` too.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2970127753/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3308799352","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107481#issuecomment-3308799352","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107481","id":3308799352,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FOEV4","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-18T17:51:08Z","updated_at":"2025-09-18T17:51:08Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3308799352/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confuse